  "term": "cognitive plasticity",
  "definition": "Cognitive plasticity is the mind’s ability to improve or change cognitive performance through experience or training. In the source, it refers to older adults’ capacity to strengthen functions such as attention and alertness in ways that may help offset age-related decline.",
